<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador posts $148 mln trade surplus in August.</title>
<headline>Ecuador posts $148 mln trade surplus in August.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador reported a trade surplus of $148 million for August, up from $44 million in the same month last year, the Central Bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Exports reached $400 million, up from the $387 million in August 1995. Imports fell to $252 million from $343 million.</p>
<p>In the first eight months of 1996, Ecuador had a trade surplus of $839 million, up from $187 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom 5932 258433</p>
</text>
